  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "Hi Dr. Smith. I guess I'm here because... well, I've started doing things at work and school lately that just don't really make sense. Like, at work—I do bookkeeping—I've been taking all the receipts and just lining them up all the way across the floor. We get so many receipts from this one hardware store, and they use that weird thermal paper, you know? The kind that turns black if you scratch it with your fingernail. I used to do that all the time when I was a kid when my mom would take me to the grocery store. I'd draw little smiley faces on the back of the receipt while she was loading the car. She always used those canvas bags way before it was a trendy thing to do... \n\nBut yeah, I just line them up on the floor. Or I'll sit at my desk and just tap the calculator in sets of nine. Always nine. And then sometimes I'll go over and just stand by the copier with my hands held up in the air, just frozen there, until someone finally walks by and asks if I'm okay. It's a really old copier, actually, it makes this loud humming noise and jams every time you try to print double-sided... but anyway, yeah, people have been looking at me funny because of all that.",
      "new_confirmed_symptoms": [
        "S021",
        "S022"
      ],
