    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you are lining up the receipts or tapping the calculator, do you feel an internal pressure or a sense of dread that forces you to do it, or do you feel like these actions are being controlled by some outside force?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "I wouldn't say it's like a dread, or like someone is physically moving my hands for me... it's more about what the numbers actually mean. I know it sounds strange, but I get convinced that certain invoice totals, account numbers, and due dates are actually hidden messages about me. I have to line up the receipts to see them clearly. \n\nMy supervisor, Mr. Davis—he's been at the company forever and he always wears these really loud patterned ties. Like yesterday, he had one with tiny golf clubs all over it, and he doesn't even play golf. He told me he prefers fishing out by the lake on the weekends, usually for bass, though he says the lake has been getting too crowded lately with all those jet skis... anyway, he sits down with me and tries to show me that they are just normal accounting entries. He pulls up the master spreadsheet and points at the columns to prove it. But even when he shows me they are normal, I still feel like they are tracking whether I understand the pattern. \n\nWhich makes me think about tracking numbers, you know? Like when you order a package. I bought this vintage desk lamp on eBay a couple weeks ago, the kind with the green glass shade, like they use in old libraries or banks. The tracking said it was delivered but it took me three days to find it because the mailman put it behind the bushes near the side gate, and it rained, so the cardboard got all mushy. But yeah, I just tap the calculator because I need to figure out the pattern they're sending me.",
      "new_confirmed_symptoms": [
        "S019",
        "S021"
      ],
