    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever heard voices or sounds that other people around you cannot hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I... I do hear things sometimes. Like when I'm just sitting alone at my desk, or when I'm walking home from my night classes. It's usually a man's voice, and it sounds so real. He'll say things like, \"check line seven,\" or \"you missed the sign.\" It's so clear that I actually stop and look around, but the street is always empty. \n\nWalking home at night is actually pretty nice, usually. The air gets cooler, and you can smell the jasmine from Mrs. Gable's yard at the corner. She has this huge bush that just takes over the whole fence. She used to give out full-sized candy bars on Halloween, which made her house the best one on the block. But last year she switched to those little boxes of raisins, which, honestly, nobody wants. I mean, they just get stuck in your teeth, and the boxes always get squished at the bottom of the bag. But her garden is still really nice. \n\nAnyway, yeah, I look around and there's nobody there, just the voice telling me I missed a sign.",
